{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109431","id":2731010411,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6ix-lr","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109431","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109431.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109431.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109431","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109431/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109431/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109431/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/093d1919097c910075532eebf510d5ceefbb4138","number":109431,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Make `OpenXRCompositionLayer` and its children safe for multithreaded rendering","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Presently, our implementation of OpenXR composition layers is not thread-safe when used with `rendering/driver/threads/thread_model` set to \"Separate\".\r\n\r\nThis can lead to crashes. For example, if you run [this fork of the GDQuest TPS demo](https://github.com/dsnopek/gdquest-tps-demo/tree/standalone-vr-slush-multithreaded) and rapidly press the \"Y\" button (which will toggle visibility of a composition layer with performance info) it will eventually crash. (NOTE: this is easier to reproduce with the OpenGL renderer, but in order to use that on Quest or other Android-based headsets, you'll need to use PR #109080)\r\n\r\n**This PR fixes that crash and makes OpenXR composition layers thread-safe in general!**\r\n\r\nI've tested this with a litany of demo projects, covering all types of composition layers including using Android surfaces, on both Vulkan and OpenGL, as well as with both single and multi-threaded rendering. Everything seems to be working fine for me!\r\n\r\nI tried really hard to not totally rewrite how we handle OpenXR composition layers, and did a couple of earlier iterations that made smaller changes, but I wasn't able to make it fully thread-safe without going all the way to Godot's \"server pattern\" and using `OpenXRCompositionLayerExtension` as a proxy to the underlying resources using `RID`s. So, unfortunately, the diff is pretty big and not the easiest to review. However, long-term, I think this is a much cleaner and easier-to-maintain design.\r\n\r\n~~**NOTE:** This is currently marked as DRAFT because it builds upon PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108644. I did this, because that PR was already ready to go, and I don't want to cause merge conflicts for the first-time contributor who made it. :-) I'll take this out of DRAFT after that PR is merged~~","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,